INT. ROOFTOP GREENHOUSE RESTAURANT - NIGHT

Candles in jam jars. Fairy lights. A single table set for two among rows of tomato plants. The city glitters beyond the glass.

NAOMI ABERFORTH-KANE (30s, silk dress, nervous hands) adjusts a fork. Straightens it. Looks at the empty chair.

Footsteps. TEODOR VASILEV-OSEI (30s, rumpled suit, a bouquet of grocery-store carnations) skids around the corner of a tomato row.

TEODOR
I'm late.

NAOMI
You're eleven minutes late.

TEODOR
Eleven. Not twelve.

NAOMI
Eleven and a half.

He holds out the carnations. She stares at them. Then, helplessly, smiles. He sits. They look at each other across the candle.

NAOMI (CONT'D)
You came.

TEODOR
Of course I came.

NAOMI
Last time you didn't.

TEODOR
Last time my mother was in the hospital.

NAOMI
I know. I'm sorry. I just--

TEODOR
No. It's fair.

She puts her napkin in her lap. He picks up the menu without opening it. They both laugh at the same moment, then stop.

A WAITER in a green apron glides up, notepad ready. He is very young, very solemn.

WAITER
Good evening. Is this a celebration?

NAOMI
Maybe.

TEODOR
Possibly.

WAITER
I'll bring something special.

He glides off. Naomi covers her mouth. Teodor reaches across and takes her hand. She lets him.

NAOMI
(whispering)
He's going to bring us a cake.

TEODOR
He's going to bring us a cake.

Then Naomi's face changes. She looks over his shoulder, past the tomato plants, at the stairwell door.

NAOMI (CONT'D)
Teodor.

TEODOR
What?

NAOMI
Don't turn around.

He turns around. In the doorway, a WOMAN in a red coat stands very still, a suitcase at her feet.

TEODOR
Marisol.

The Waiter returns with a tiny cake and a single candle. He stops, takes in the scene, and quietly sets the cake in the middle of the table. Nobody touches it.
